}}The bronze ''Lovers'' given to [[University of Melbourne|Melbourne University]] by Boyd and housed in the fourth floor bridge in the [[John Medley Building]], was stolen and never been recovered. Boyd provided a replacement, a bather figure for the east garden of University House.<ref name=":3">{{Cite journal|last=Sloggett|first=Robyn|date=December 2011|title=Sculpture in the grounds, with some memories of things that got away|url=https://museumsandcollections.unimelb.edu.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0011/1378955/03_Robyn-Sloggett.pdf|journal=University of Melbourne Collections|issue=9|pages=3–11}}</ref>

